# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Current Locks
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A long island cut by a straight canal with three iron lock gates, a crank for each on the bank: the way the engine's water once ran south. A keeper's rules, a deep basin, a bear's den and a kitchen garden.
island on.arrive=message||A canal, straight as a rule, through the whole island - and three iron gates across it, shut.

story lock1|Lock 1 open|Hinge|You wound open the first lock on Current Locks.
story lock2|Lock 2 open|Hinge|You wound open the second lock on Current Locks.
story lock3|Lock 3 open|Hinge|You wound open the last lock on Current Locks. The canal runs free to the sea.

note lockrules Lock keeper's rules | LOCK KEEPER'S RULES\n\n1. Locks open in order. One, two, three. Never three first.\n2. Keep the basin clear. The anglers come up the canal at night.\n3. Feed the bear nothing. It lives by lock 2 and it thinks it owns lock 2.\n4. The canal carries the engine's water to the ring. When the ring stops asking, close the gates and go home.\n\nThe ring stopped asking.
note inesnote Ines's note | INES - in neat small letters, on a page torn from her radio log\n\nThe engine has three rings. I have seen this before. In the Commons.\n\nThe same sign - a ring cut by three waves - was on the doors of the Hearth there, under the sea. The Commons drew it for luck. I think the people who built this drew it first, and we copied it without knowing what it meant, the way children copy a word.\n\nThe pulse is clear enough now to write down. Three beats, a pause, three beats. It is a station call. Station 1. Somebody down there is calling a crew, and somebody up here is answering every time.\n\nHedda has gone to the smelters. I go to the spire. If you are following us: thank you. It is easier to be brave with someone behind you.
note lockhouse Lock house | The lock house chest: a wind turbine's plans, flapping in the draught.
note basinchest Basin chest | A chest on the basin floor, half buried: an advanced battery's plans, sealed in wax.
note denchest Bear den | Under the bear's bedding: a headlamp's plans, chewed at one corner.
note kitchen Keeper's kitchen | The keeper's kitchen chest: an electric grill's plans and a sack of seeds and roots.
loot lockhouse Blueprint_WindTurbine*1;Scrap*4;Plank*6
prop lockhouse loot.refill=0
loot basinchest Blueprint_BatteryAdvanced*1;CopperOre*2;Battery*1
prop basinchest loot.refill=0
loot denchest Blueprint_HeadLight_Advanced*1;Leather*2;Scrap*2
prop denchest loot.refill=0
loot kitchen Blueprint_ElectricGrill*1;Raw_Beet*2;Raw_Potato*2;Seed_Pineapple*2;Seed_Watermelon*2;Seed_Strawberry*2
prop kitchen loot.refill=0

prop crank1 beh.use=Wind lock 1's crank
prop crank1 if.use=!signal|lock1
prop crank1 on.use=signal||lock1\ngive||story:lock1*1\nhide|gate1\nmessage||The crank turns, chains rattle in the posts and the first gate sinks into the canal. The water starts to move.\nsound||event:/raft/engine/waterwheel
prop crank1 else.use=message||Lock 1 is open.
prop crank2 beh.use=Wind lock 2's crank
prop crank2 if.use=signal|lock1\n!signal|lock2
prop crank2 on.use=signal||lock2\ngive||story:lock2*1\nhide|gate2\nmessage||The second gate drops. The canal runs faster.\nsound||event:/raft/engine/waterwheel
prop crank2 else.use=message||Locks open in order - or this one is open already.
prop crank3 beh.use=Wind lock 3's crank
prop crank3 if.use=signal|lock2\n!signal|lock3
prop crank3 on.use=signal||lock3\ngive||story:lock3*1\nhide|gate3\nmessage||The last gate sinks. The whole canal pours south into the sea with a roar - toward the smoke.\nsound||event:/raft/engine/waterwheel
prop crank3 else.use=message||Locks open in order - or this one is open already.

note keeperspares Lock-keeper's spares | The lock-keepers' spare-parts chest: hinges, bolts, a bar of iron.
loot keeperspares Hinge*3;Bolt*4;MetalIngot*2;Rope*2
note lockrota Lock-keepers' rota | ROTA - pinned inside a box lid\n\nGate 1: Mira. Gate 2: Old Jonas. Gate 3: nobody since Jonas's son left for the Fleet.\n\nUnder it, a running argument in two hands:\n\nMira: Jonas, the bear is in your gate again.\nJonas: The bear IS my gate now. I have made my peace with it.\nMira: You fed it.\nJonas: Once. It looked hungry.\nMira: It always looks hungry. It is a bear.\n\nAt the bottom, newer, in a careful old hand: Gates wound, oiled, left for the next ones. The bear remembers me. - S.W.
note lockcavechest Old canal chest | A chest left on a ledge above the old water line: the first lock keeper's tools.
prop lockcavechest loot.refill=0
note diggerlist Diggers' roll | CANAL DIGGERS' ROLL - nailed inside the bunkhouse door\n\nForty-one names, crossed out one by one as the crews went home. Beside one, a heart. Beside another, a pig, which may be a joke about the man or about his cooking.\n\nAt the bottom, in the foreman's hand: The canal is not for boats. It carries the current south to the Engine. Do not let the locks rust.\n\nAnd under that, smaller: The Engine went to standby the year we finished. Nobody told us why. We stayed on another season out of pride and then we went home too. If anyone ever asks, we did a good job. Tell them we did a good job.
note canalplanelog Canal plane log | SURVEY PLANE LOG - the canal run\n\nThe canal points due south to within half a degree. So does the pulse. So did the beacon. Every station on this line is aimed at the same place, like the spokes of a wheel round a hub nobody visits.\n\nForced down in the north-west. Walking to the locks. The bear watched me the whole way and did nothing, which was worse.\n\nWe never dug toward the sea. Every cut points at the Engine in the south - the canal was its drain. And the smoke in the south, over the dark island, is the stormworks still burning. Nobody has fed those furnaces in forty years. Somebody has.
# (deep pass 10-24: the climb and the dive)
story dredgekey|Dredge key|Bolt|The dredge gantry's key, floated up to the grate in the old lock chamber when the three wheels let the water in.
note cldivechest Lock chamber grate | The water lifted the dredge key into the grate.
loot cldivechest story:dredgekey*1;Rope*2;Scrap*3;Bolt*2
prop cldivechest loot.refill=0
note cltop Dredge gantry locker | The dredge key turns: the gantry tools and the last orders.
loot cltop TitaniumOre*2;Battery*1;CircuitBoard*1
prop cltop loot.refill=0
prop cltop obj.name=cltop
prop cltop if.open=has|story:dredgekey|1
prop cltop else.open=message||The dredge gantry's locker. A keyhole shaped like a dredge bucket.
note clstash Gantry stash | A keeper's bag of rivets and a fuse.
loot clstash Battery*1;CircuitBoard*1;Nail*6
prop clstash loot.refill=0
note cldivesecret Van strongbox | The canal toll box, still locked. Its hinges are not.
loot cldivesecret MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;Rope*1
prop cldivesecret loot.refill=0
note clcairn Gantry cairn | A cairn on the bank peak, the lock keeper's spanner on top:\n\nThree wheels, one key. Let the water do the lifting. - J.
prop cldivechest if.open=signal|lw1\nsignal|lw2\nsignal|lw3
prop cldivechest else.open=message||The grate is barred. Three sluice wheels round the chamber hold the bar down - turn them all.
note keepercl Keeper's log: Locks | KEEPER'S LOG. Current Locks - oilcloth, under a stone by lock 3, a little chewed:\n\nI am tired tonight, love, so I will write it plain.\n\nThe Engine is asleep. Your crew put it to bed and never came up, and the Concord called it standby and took the boats away. I have heard your call every night for forty years. Station 1, crew to posts. Station 1, crew to posts.\n\nSo I am bringing you a crew. Five posts want five pairs of hands. I have one pair, and they shake. The pilgrims have six, and good boots.\n\nWhen the Engine wakes, the Well opens. When the Well opens, you come home. That is all I want. I do not care what else it wakes.\n\nCalling. Calling.\n\n- Silas
note heddacl Hedda's note: the kitchen | HEDDA - on the back of a seed packet, left in the keeper's kitchen\n\nAte the lock keeper's beets. Left him seeds. Fair trade, and the beets were terrible.\n\nInes thinks the old man is answering a woman down in the Well. She found his initials on the lock rota, and his wife's name in every log he leaves. Wren. Silas and Mara. I found something too, and I have not told her: he does not just follow the pulse. He makes the masts carry it. He wants it loud.\n\nI go south to the smoke, to the Stormworks, to see what he lit the furnaces for. Ines goes to the cooling spire to listen. Whoever you are, come to the smelters. I could use the company, and Teo is not here to complain for me.
quest title=Three Locks
quest intro=A canal with three shut gates. Go to the first lock.
step reach|lock_1|1|Go to lock 1
step read|Lock keeper's rules|1|Read the lock keeper's rules on the gate post
step blueprint|Blueprint_WindTurbine|1|Take the wind turbine plans from the lock house
step collect|story:lock1|1|Wind lock 1's crank
step kill|Angler fish|3|Clear the anglers out of the basin under lock 1
step blueprint|Blueprint_BatteryAdvanced|1|Take the battery plans from the chest on the basin floor
step collect|story:lock2|1|Wind lock 2's crank
step kill|Bear|1|Drive the bear away from lock 2
step blueprint|Blueprint_HeadLight_Advanced|1|Take the headlamp plans from the bear's den
step collect|story:lock3|1|Wind lock 3's crank
step reach|locksridge|1|Climb the west ridge above the canal
step read|Canal plane log|1|Read the log at the plane wreck in the north-west
step open|Fuel crate|1|Find the fuel crate by the canal plane
step open|Engine room locker|1|Start the dredge engine by the bunkhouse in the south and open its locker
step reach|cl_dive|1|Dive into the old lock chamber
step collect|story:dredgekey|1|Take the dredge key from the grate
step blueprint|Blueprint_ElectricGrill|1|Take the electric grill plans from the keeper's kitchen
quest done=The canal runs free. Down it, south, smoke over a dark island - and the clang of a smelter.
quest reward=Seed_Mango*2;Scrap*6;Rope*4

save Current Locks
